  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Indigo sereno",
    "overview": "Plancito is calm in a business that is not. A reseller opens it between WhatsApp chats with three renewals due and a customer asking for a password; the interface answers with order: soft paper backgrounds, one confident indigo, and only the urgent things in color. It is a modern, professional SaaS whose restraint balances the friendly diminutive of the name. Warmth comes from Spanish copy, rounded touch targets and generous spacing, not from decoration.\n\nThe system splits its temperament by surface. The **panel** (dashboard, customers, subscriptions, mother accounts, profile) is operational and sober: dense enough to scan, flat, with indigo reserved for action, selection and the one hero figure. **Public and customer-facing surfaces** (landing, customer portal, public promotions) may be more expressive: larger display type, entrance motion, richer brand washes. Both speak the same tokens.\n\nIt must not look like a generic Ant Design admin (grey tables, dark sidebar, default chrome without character) or like a cold fintech dashboard (corporate distance, chart walls). Plancito is close to the person using it.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Mobile-first: bottom navigation, FAB, bottom sheets, safe-area aware; the sidebar appears from `md` up.",
      "One brand hue (indigo) on Papel/Carbón slate neutrals; semantic colors only for state.",
      "Flat by default: borders and tonal layers, no shadows except on things that float.",
      "Inter everywhere; heavy weights (700–800) and tight tracking for figures and titles.",
      "Full light/dark parity via surface/content tokens that flip on `.dark`."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Tokens-Only Rule",
        "body": "Components use the surface/content tokens (`bg-surface`, `bg-surface-muted`, `border-border`, `text-content`, `text-content-muted`, `text-content-subtle`, `text-brand-ink`), never raw slate hex, so dark mode and rebranding stay a token edit in `src/index.css` mirrored in `antd-provider.tsx`.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Voice Rule",
        "body": "Indigo is the only brand hue in the panel. Violet (`#8B5CF6`) exists as an accent token but stays out of panel chrome; it lives in promotion templates and the `migrated` status only.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Color Means State Rule",
        "body": "Red, amber, green and blue appear only when they say something about a subscription, slot, payment or error. Never as decoration.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Ink Rule",
        "body": "Colored text and icons always use an `-ink` token or `text-brand-ink`, never a 500 tone: `text-success` on white is 2.3:1. Every text pair passes AA (4.5:1) in both themes.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Weight-Not-Size Rule",
